WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:06.980
Previously on 
The Reflection

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:19.820
Nina...

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.950
Mom!

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.620
Why would you do this?

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.870
It's all for the plan.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.380
What is this plan?

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.670
What the... What the hell was that for?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.350
You're basically a lighthouse.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:42.310
You're a mindless light that attracts 
and lures out those with abilities.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.720
Shut up!

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:51.060
I... talked to Wraith.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.620
They said they need my ability.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.290
You can turn off the lamp 
in the lighthouse now...

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.570
Hollow King.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.490
<i>Ian... What are you, a kid?</i>

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:04.550
<i>For crying out loud...</i>

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:10.740
<i>Are you listening, Ian? 
Aaron made something amazing.</i>

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.430
<i>Of course, we helped out, too!</i>

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.130
<i>Ian, when you get back, 
take it for a test drive.</i>

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:33.490
Someone...

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.070
Nice... Very nice!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:43.390
So long.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.060
As of today, this island is ours.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.020
G-Got it.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.950
Who the hell are you?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:34.840
Huh?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.620
Where is Wraith?

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.610
Huh? I have no idea what the 
hell you're talking about.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.220
I won't let anything be stolen from me again.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.240
I'll take care of you, right here and now.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.150
Where is Wraith?

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.000
I really don't know!

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:17.320
There's nothing to be gained from hurting him.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.360
He doesn't know anything.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:25.820
Damn it!

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.770
You called me a "lighthouse," right?

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.460
A lighthouse is just fine.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.690
But I'll only shine for Wraith.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.690
Why?

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.310
What?

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:52.870
Why are you...

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:34.170
The way you teleport isn't much different 
from the way I've been moving.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.530
You always let us go in the end.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.790
Because we weren't what you were after.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.290
It was the same earlier.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:49.110
You were after Maggie and Nina.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.690
And yet...

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.670
Why bother with me?

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.700
Because our master is...

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:00.980
I am... not having fun!

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:32.190
If you're not going to finish me off, 
why bother with me?

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.410
You won't kill me.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.520
You can't kill me.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.800
Because Wraith said not to?

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.910
I wanted to see the extent of your abilities.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:58.680
I don't understand. Why me?

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.230
What is it about me?

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:01.910
There's no need to think about it.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:04.280
That's our master's job.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:10.580
Our master has promised to envelop 
the world in darkness.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.940
Darkness?

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.790
So that everyone

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.940
will have darkness equally.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.790
If I cannot grasp the light, 
let darkness envelop everything.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.390
That's what I have always longed for.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:46.550
And yet you won't let me feel the darkness.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.850
Why do you seek darkness?

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:55.110
Darkness brought me back to life.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.110
3 Years Ago

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:00.370
3 Years Ago
Detroit, America 
2:00 AM

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.570
Someone...

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.180
I can't even begin to imagine

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:41.770
the kind of world you've 
experienced until now.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:44.880
But I've always thought

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:50.240
that even in darkness, someone would 
take my hand and guide me.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.830
Let darkness embrace you.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:06.600
So are you implying that it was 
X-On who took your hand?

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:09.080
I don't know.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.780
You and I might actually be alike.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:22.610
But our master will never let go of my hand.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:26.270
I won't allow it.

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.250
Wraith is trying to...

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.990
The ones we acquired in New Orleans...

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.770
They will be released.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:54.940
In return, Eleanor, I would have you 
accept my master's invitation.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:57.650
Come to us.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:00.150
You'll release them?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:06.150
I can't help but wonder if you 
are truly worth that trade.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.660
But it's what my master desires.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:15.010
Will you ask X-On for the answer, as usual?

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.240
He only has answers for himself.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:22.600
Unlike my master, he will not lead you.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.430
He'll only use you.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:29.880
What do you know about him?

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.770
He won't save his friends.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:44.450
But you can save about 
thirty others like you.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.510
Let us meet here again at dawn.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.680
Narita International Airport

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.270
Honestly, what are you doing?

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.570
Didn't you bring too much?

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.400
That's why it's sticking out.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.160
Well, doesn't it make you anxious 
to be without certain things?

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.010
It'd actually fit if you'd 
just organize everything.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.250
This vehicle...

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.510
How long have you been monitoring us?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.200
There's not much point in answering that.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.690
We've just been waiting for an opportunity.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:54.360
We've decided that this is the 
moment to make our move.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.560
So in New Orleans... and San Antonio...

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:05.110
When people were abducted, you just 
sat there watching and did nothing?

00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:08.820
Who are you people?

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:13.340
The Reflected woman you met with...

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:17.520
We're following the movements of 
the group she's involved with.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.830
That's all I can say now.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:20.080
That's not true!

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:21.840
You also mean us, don't you?

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:28.830
After the Reflection, our team was established 
and granted federal authority.

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:30.560
We have no official name.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:36.350
We're just here to monitor you, keep a 
cautious eye on you, and act when needed.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.790
Pardon my bluntness.

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.500
That sounds like a cursory response.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.110
Our most urgent assignment

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:49.330
is to figure out what this Wraith is plotting.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:51.440
That's what we're trying to do, too.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.450
Then... let us help.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.510
Help?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:57.620
We heard your conversation earlier.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.370
You were listening in?

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.880
Would you consider accepting her invitation?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.130
To be a decoy?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.770
We'll fully back you up.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.660
I want you to find out what their goal is.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:20.200
If you put this anywhere on your clothes,
we'll be able to hear you.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.970
Didn't she mention

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:25.650
that they'd release the 
people they've abducted?

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:29.690
Are you trying to use that 
as part of the deal, tol?

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.290
That's not my intention.

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:37.360
I know that you can't just 
accept their terms.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.590
And the fact that it might be a trap.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:41.660
Would you consider it, even knowing that?

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:44.920
Are you

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.820
connected to X-On?

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:49.500
Does he know about this?

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.340
He doesn't.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:54.430
We have a deal to meet only 
when our interests align.

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:58.490
We've taken into custody some of 
the Reflected he's captured,

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.430
and we sometimes share information.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:03.370
Just who is he?

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.190
I can't reveal any more.

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.440
Rather, we don't know.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:39.590
So you knew?

00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:42.220
Now, those are cursory documents.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.900
They aren't cursory to me.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.740
We need your cooperation!

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.700
Think about this carefully.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.910
Ow!

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:05.230
I guess you can't control your 
powers very well yet.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.420
That's why...

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.420
Please make me your student!

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:13.370
I thought that you were using your powers

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:15.600
for good, without any hesitation.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:18.730
You knew the meaning of power.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:23.060
And, um... I thought you were a decent person.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:27.310
I... I'm sorry.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:30.150
I want you to tell me

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.250
exactly what my powers are.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:35.940
Why I was allowed to live 
and given these powers...

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:36.920
Sorry.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:38.570
I'm not feeling it.

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:43.970
But if you don't want to die, 
you should hide somewhere.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.220
There's nowhere that I can!

00:17:49.370 --> 00:17:51.880
I have nowhere to go.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.230
Well, there are two kids here.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:56.680
Yeah, I know.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:58.920
I am a kid, after all.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.650
Don't look at me.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.730
What a coincidence.

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:20.180
That's a lie. You were looking for me.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:22.840
Well, I mean... Things got kinda awkward.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.720
I don't get it.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.640
What am I to you, exactly?

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.480
A decoy?

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.980
Or bait?

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:41.050
Well, if I'm bait, I need to be 
somewhere you can see me.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.520
That's why you came to find me, right?

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:47.220
Don't go quiet like that.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.560
I have nothing to say.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.570
The metal woman said you 
wouldn't save your friends.

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.300
She gave me these weird documents...

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.320
Documents I don't understand.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:07.200
Twenty years ago, an incident 
occurred at a certain facility,

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.190
and it burned up in a fire.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.190
Apparently, there were a lot of victims.

00:19:12.190 --> 00:19:14.130
Even children.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.820
In the official release, 
they said there was one survivor.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:21.810
But someone was listed as missing 
in an investigative report.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:27.350
Who was the boy called "X"?

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.350
Was that boy the survivor?

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:36.610
Was that you?

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.610
Say something!

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:44.350
I've had enough...

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:49.690
Did you let your friends die?

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.130
That's exactly right.

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:58.110
Am I your friend?

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:02.230
I'm weak... I can't do anything.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.340
But...

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:09.010
I can't just abandon people 
I might be able to save!

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:32.500
Good work.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:36.320
Care to join me? Have a seat.

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:41.010
Or do you not want to wrinkle 
that fancy government-issued suit?

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.760
You're no ordinary detective, are you?

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.710
Don't overestimate me.

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.770
I'm just a drunkard detective.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:52.290
Two of you are missing.

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:54.270
He's out looking for someone

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:56.080
this late at night.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.770
He said he was worried about a friend.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:05.530
She had documents about 
the incident at the facility.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:10.790
For crying out loud... 
Does privacy not exist anymore?

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.620
I just saw her.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.290
Did she say anything?

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:20.790
She asked me if I let my friends die.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.360
You...

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.810
I told her she was exactly right.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.120
B-But that was...

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.870
We all decided on that.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:31.450
So no one should have any regrets!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:35.270
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:40.910
She's planning to go to Wraith.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:47.370
In exchange for all of the Reflected 
that were taken in New Orleans.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:49.430
It's a trap.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:51.690
There's no way they'll keep their word!

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:35.250
Miss, would you prefer beef or fish?

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:37.050
Crap. She's speaking English.

00:22:37.050 --> 00:22:38.000
What should we do?

00:22:39.310 --> 00:22:40.820
Does "fish" mean sashimi?

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:42.000
Of course not!

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:44.510
Ugh, I just can't decide!

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:46.620
What should we do?

00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:48.260
But...

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:51.260
We have to decide!

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Next Time 
Downtown L.A.

00:24:48.050 --> 00:24:55.010
Narration: Stan Lee
